ip. Weaknesses: unfriendly, eats unhealthily, not good at taking criticism, unorganized, show-off.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: arrogant, weak leadership, moody, loner.\n\nWe need to weigh for long-distance pilot: reliability, technical competence, calm under pressure, decision-making speed, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nReliability: C (100% reliable), B (conscientious), A (anticipates danger), D (responsibility). Decision speed: C (quick correct decisions), A (sees complex connections), D (solves problems extremely well), B unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: B (weather, computer), C (understands complicated tech, attention), A (spatial vision, complex connections), D (problem solving, concentration).\n\nCalm under pressure: B (handles stress), C (keeps calm in crisis - from original list), D (responds adequately), A (anticipates dangerous situations maybe proactive).\n\nTeamwork/communication: C (positive atmosphere, concern for others) but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric. B (negative attitude). A (unfriendly, show-off). D (loner, moody, arrogant).\n\nProfessional development: B (computer skills maybe up-to-date), C not willing to further education, A not open to new ideas, D unknown.\n\nThus C seems strongest overall: reliability, decision speed, crew atmosphere, concern for others, technical understanding. Weaknesses are communication difficulty and egocentric, but positive atmosphere suggests some teamwork. B's unknown decision speed is a big gap; his attitude issues are significant.\n\nThus I think I should shift to Candidate C. Provide confidence maybe 70%. Mention uncertainties: C's communication issues impact, B's decision speed unknown, etc. Also note that if we get evidence that B makes decisions quickly and works well with crew, could shift.\n\nThus produce public message accordingly."}
